"Many kept-up but empty buildings on the grounds are hidden, unused for a century or more."
"The Spire folds them into higher dimensions; their glyphs warp one's sense of distance and time."
"Nivordin Lecture Hall is folded into oblivion; inside, it is as large as the main arena."
"The Spire holds a chained augera in a crystal dodecahedron; it powers the wall wards and arena."
"The Spire weighs all who enter and opens its upper doors only to those it permits."
"The Vault lies beneath the Lower Library: originals kept for millennia, some older than the Empire."
"Not even sages enter the Vault; its ornate door opens to the Demiurge's staff, at his will alone."
"Vault copies bear a ward of secrecy and notes may not leave; public encyclopedias are edited."
"Wysana are intelligent constructs of pure arcana; the Fateweavers let the Demiurge make a few."
"The Demiurge's nameless wysana is bound to his staff and runs the library cafe and campus services."
"The wysana works through oblivion: it fetches, cooks and moves goods unseen, and fights if bidden."
"The Demiurge must work with the Fateweavers; Caldwell calls himself their loyal opposition."
"The professors play a game with students as pieces; its winner picks the next Demiurge."
"Kant and Reeves have Fateweaver ties; Kant wants Caden Dundale gone but may not act himself."
"The Fateweavers have tapered Academy enrolment for a very long time."
"The school turned to war training because of the Chosen One's Prophecy, on Caldwell's advice."
"Reeves wiped the Chosen One's identity and the Prophecy's words from all minds, using the Spire."
"The lake door is folded slightly into a higher dimension; seniors pass on the trick to open it."
"A Minor Control Sphere's open command reveals the lake door; the marble melts back from old wood."
"A wild augera haunted the lake; it wore the face of Jerric's drowned mother and kept him alive."
"This winter the Chosen One and his friends broke the lake augera; its core is in Emilia."
"Fragments of the lake augera went into the others; one is spliced into Devon Ka'atryn's flare."
"A stranger calling himself of no known nation now speaks from reflections in the lake."
"The arena shuts down runaway arcanophany; only the Demiurge could break its barriers."
"The Demiurge seems to teleport; in truth he phases by folding oblivion around himself."
"Caldwell tutors Caden Dundale privately in the arena and the Vault in return for a future favour."
"The Spire augera may not speak to Caden Dundale unless he speaks first, by the Demiurge's binding."
